# Ground truth and recorded measurements. Never translate line endings.
#
# Git converts LF to CRLF on checkout on Windows by default, which changes the
# bytes and so changes the SHA-256 of every vendored file. The checksums in
# reference/CHECKSUMS.sha256 are of the exact bytes as distributed upstream, and
# the golden trace is a recorded measurement, so neither may be rewritten by a
# convenience feature. The first Windows CI run failed on precisely this.
reference/** -text
golden/** -text

# Everything else gets normalised in the repository and checked out natively.
* text=auto
